<title>USA: TABLE - Travel Ports Q4 shr $0.07 vs $0.04.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Travel Ports Q4 shr $0.07 vs $0.04.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.Y. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the quarter ended April 30</p>
<p>					   1997	     1996</p>
<p>    Revenue			 $55,763,298    $47,249,253</p>
<p>    Net income			 $423,958	 $201,690</p>
<p>    Net per share primary	     $0.07	    $0.04</p>
<p>    Net per share diluted	     $0.07	    $0.04</p>
<p>    Avg shrs primary		5,702,439	5,656,427</p>
<p>    Avg shrs diluted		7,344,725	7,315,662</p>
<p>				     For the year ended April 30</p>
<p>					   1997	     1996</p>
<p>    Revenue			$207,103,805   $165,164,391</p>
<p>    Net income		     $1,700,205     $1,690,500</p>
<p>    Net per share primary	     $0.30	    $0.30</p>
<p>    Net per share diluted	     $0.26	    $0.26</p>
<p>    Avg shrs primary		5,704,259	5,681,718</p>
<p>    Avg shrs diluted		7,376,416	7,361,868</p>
<p>NOTES: Full company name is Travel Ports of America Inc.</p>
<p>Q4 same store revenues were up $1,139,000 or 2.5 percent versus a year ago.</p>
<p>The majority of the Q4 revenue increase came from new stores in Baltimore and Harborcreek, Pa.</p>
<p>Revenues for the year were 25 percent greater than the prior year. Revenues on a same store basis increased 8 percent over a year ago.</p>
